## Claude Platform on AWS

With the provider's `aws` block this resource is **unverified**: the [platform page](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-platform-on-aws) and the release notes of 2026-10-14 announce scheduled deployments, but the gateway's [route table](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/claude-platform-on-aws-iam-actions), which denies any route it does not list, does not list `/v1/deployments`. If the gateway refuses the route, the operation fails and leaves the state untouched.

There, each run creates its session as an IAM role of your AWS account ([scheduled deployments](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/scheduled-deployments)). Creating a deployment for an agent whose execution identity is not an `aws_role` returns a 400. The role's trust policy must let the `aws-external-anthropic.amazonaws.com` service principal call `sts:AssumeRole` and `sts:SetSourceIdentity`, the role needs `aws-external-anthropic:CreateSession`, `sts:GetWebIdentityToken` and `sts:TagGetWebIdentityToken`, and whoever sets the role on the agent needs `iam:PassRole` on it, in the same account. `anthropic_agent` does not manage the execution identity yet: set it outside Terraform.

